# Enhancement Three: Databases

## Artifact
Grazioso Salvare Animal Shelter Dashboard — originally developed for CS 340.

## Overview
This project uses Python and MongoDB to manage animal shelter records and support a dashboard for searching and filtering animals.

## Enhancements
For my CS 499 capstone, I improved the database portion of the project by adding environment-variable configuration for database credentials, connection testing, input validation, a compound MongoDB index, and an aggregation query for breed-based summaries.

## Purpose
These changes focus on database security, data integrity, query organization, and maintainability. The compound index is intended to improve filtering performance, although I did not complete a before-and-after performance benchmark.

## Included Files
- Original CS 340 project ZIP
- Enhanced CS 499 project ZIP
- Enhancement Three narrative document

## Testing and Future Improvements
The narrative discusses the enhancements and their testing limitations. Future work includes comparing query execution plans with MongoDB explain() and testing against an authenticated database environment.
